HST Office: the Print page of the File panel shows one print panel however often it is opened (Linux).

Each job on the Print page gets its own panel form of the print dialog (PrintDialog with a parent container,
vcl::PrintJobPanel); when the job ends (the File panel closes, another page, "More Options..." cancelled) the panel
is destroyed and the next job builds a new one. On gtk3 the widgets a builder put into a container stay in it after
the builder is gone (GtkInstanceBuilder only drops its GtkBuilder), so every opening of the page added one more
panel under the old ones, each with its printer box, settings and preview, about 20 MB a time; 1.0.2 showed 2, 3,
... panels in Writer, Sheets, Slides and Draw. The VCL backends (Windows, macOS, gen) dispose the widgets and were
not affected. The panel now leaves its host as it is destroyed, as SfxTabPage does.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-repeat.py (the page opened again and again in the four applications).
---
--- a/vcl/source/window/printdlg.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/window/printdlg.cxx
@@ -948,7 +948,13 @@
 void PrintDialog::ImplDestroy()
 {
     if (!m_xDialog) // the panel expands both sections; the dialog keeps its own choice
+    {
+        // The panel leaves its host container: on gtk3 the widgets a builder put into a container
+        // stay there after the builder is gone, so the next job's panel was shown below this one.
+        if (std::unique_ptr<weld::Container> xHost = m_xPanel->weld_parent())
+            xHost->move(m_xPanel.get(), nullptr);
         return;
+    }
     std::shared_ptr<comphelper::ConfigurationChanges> batch(comphelper::ConfigurationChanges::create());
     officecfg::Office::Common::Print::Dialog::RangeSectionExpanded::set(mxRangeExpander->get_expanded(), batch);
     officecfg::Office::Common::Print::Dialog::LayoutSectionExpanded::set(mxLayoutExpander->get_expanded(), batch);
